            <ArticleTitle>Total occlusion of the left main coronary artery in a Hong Kong Chinese.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>227-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Total occlusion of the left main coronary artery (LMCA) is a rare finding in patients with stable angina pectoris. To the best of our knowledge, it has not been described in Hong Kong Chinese before. In this paper, we report the clinical and angiographic findings of a Hong Kong Chinese with this condition treated in our unit.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
